{
    "info": {
        "_postman_id": "8f6f2b6e-2f2e-4c1a-9b9a-2b7c0e9a5b21",
        "name": "Kardux Battle API",
        "description": "Local, importable Postman collection for the Kardux Battle REST surface. Mirrors `API-TESTING.md` at the repo root exactly (same bodies, same headers, same expected responses/error cases). Replaced the project's earlier Bruno collection — see `docs/adr/0005-api-docs-and-http-client.md` for why.\n\nHow to use:\n1. Import this file and `kardux-local.postman_environment.json` (same folder).\n2. Select the \"Kardux Battle - Local\" environment (top-right dropdown).\n3. Start the API: `pnpm --filter @kardux/api dev`.\n4. Run \"1. Auth / Create a guest identity\" first — its test script auto-saves the returned `token` into the `token` collection variable, so every authenticated request below just works.",
        "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
    },
    "variable": [
        { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:3000", "type": "string" },
        { "key": "token", "value": "", "type": "string" }
    ],
    "item": [
        {
            "name": "1. Auth",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "Create a guest identity",
                    "event": [
                        {
                            "listen": "test",
                            "script": {
                                "type": "text/javascript",
                                "exec": [
                                    "const status = pm.response.code;",
                                    "pm.test('Status code is 201', function () {",
                                    "    pm.expect(status).to.equal(201);",
                                    "});",
                                    "",
                                    "if (status === 201) {",
                                    "    const response = pm.response.json();",
                                    "    if (response.token) {",
                                    "        pm.collectionVariables.set('token', response.token);",
                                    "        console.log('Saved response.json().token to the \"token\" collection variable.');",
                                    "    }",
                                    "}"
                                ]
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"nickname\": \"RafArenas\",\n  \"avatarSeed\": \"RafArenas\",\n  \"tabId\": \"3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6\"\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/guest",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["auth", "guest"]
                        },
                        "description": "No auth required. Mints a guest JWT for a brand-new player (no account, no password). `tabId` must be a UUID — any valid one works for manual testing; generate more with `node -e \"console.log(crypto.randomUUID())\"` for several fake players.\n\nOn success (201) the test script above extracts `response.json().token` and stores it as the `token` collection variable, so every other request in this collection that uses `{{token}}` picks it up automatically — no manual copy/paste needed.\n\nResponse 201:\n```json\n{\n  \"token\": \"eyJhbGciOi...\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"id\": \"clx...\",\n    \"nickname\": \"RafArenas\",\n    \"avatarSeed\": \"RafArenas\",\n    \"avatarUrl\": \"https://api.dicebear.com/9.x/adventurer/svg?seed=RafArenas\"\n  }\n}\n```"
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "2. Decks",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "List deck sources",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/decks/sources",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["decks", "sources"]
                        },
                        "description": "No auth required. Response 200: array of 10 sources. Only `\"local\"` has `\"ready\": true` today — the rest are catalog metadata (Phase 3, not built yet). `\"marvel\"` is the only one with `\"requiresApiKey\": true`."
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "3. Matches",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "Create a match - minimal",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                        "auth": {
                            "type": "bearer",
                            "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
                        },
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"visibility\": \"public\"\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/matches",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["matches"]
                        },
                        "description": "Requires auth (run \"Create a guest identity\" first so `{{token}}` is populated). Every field is optional — send `{}` to get all defaults (2-12 players, 4 packs x 8 cards, etc. — see `MatchConfig` in `docs/SPEC.md` for the full list).\n\nResponse 201:\n```json\n{\n  \"matchId\": \"clx...\",\n  \"code\": \"A3F9C1\",\n  \"status\": \"LOBBY\",\n  \"config\": { \"...\": \"full MatchConfig with defaults filled in\" },\n  \"hostId\": \"clx...\",\n  \"hostNickname\": \"RafArenas\",\n  \"hostAvatarUrl\": \"https://api.dicebear.com/9.x/adventurer/svg?seed=RafArenas\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-21T...\"\n}\n```\n\nCopy the `code` from the response — you'll need it for \"5. Match by code\" below."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Create a match - fully custom",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                        "auth": {
                            "type": "bearer",
                            "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
                        },
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"minPlayers\": 2,\n  \"maxPlayers\": 4,\n  \"autoStartPlayers\": 4,\n  \"matchDurationMs\": 600000,\n  \"visibility\": \"private\"\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/matches",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["matches"]
                        },
                        "description": "Requires auth. Same endpoint as \"Create a match - minimal\", with an explicit custom `MatchConfig` instead of relying on defaults."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Create a match - missing auth (401)",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/matches",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["matches"]
                        },
                        "description": "Deliberately sent without an `Authorization` header. Should fail with `401 ERR_UNAUTHORIZED` — useful to keep as a saved request for manual regression testing of the auth guard."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Create a match - impossible config (400)",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "POST",
                        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
                        "auth": {
                            "type": "bearer",
                            "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }]
                        },
                        "body": {
                            "mode": "raw",
                            "raw": "{\n  \"minPlayers\": 10,\n  \"maxPlayers\": 2\n}"
                        },
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/matches",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["matches"]
                        },
                        "description": "`minPlayers` > `maxPlayers` is an impossible configuration. Should fail with `400 ERR_INVALID_CONFIG` — useful to keep as a saved request for manual regression testing of the config validation."
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "4. Public matches",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "List public matches",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/matches/public",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["matches", "public"]
                        },
                        "description": "No auth required. Shows open (`visibility: \"public\"`) lobbies, newest first."
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "5. Match by code",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "Get match by code",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/matches/A3F9C1",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["matches", "A3F9C1"]
                        },
                        "description": "No auth required. Replace `A3F9C1` in the URL with a real `code` from \"Create a match - minimal\"'s response."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Get match by code - nonexistent (404)",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/matches/ZZZZZZ",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["matches", "ZZZZZZ"]
                        },
                        "description": "A code that doesn't exist. Should fail with `404 ERR_MATCH_NOT_FOUND` — useful to keep as a saved request for manual regression testing."
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "6. Leaderboard",
            "item": [
                {
                    "name": "Global leaderboard",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/leaderboard",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["leaderboard"]
                        },
                        "description": "No auth required. The dev seed (`pnpm --filter @kardux/api prisma:seed` if you haven't run it) creates 4 guest users with `LeaderboardStat` rows, so this returns real data out of the box.\n\nResponse 200:\n```json\n{\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"userId\": \"...\", \"nickname\": \"...\", \"avatarUrl\": \"...\",\n      \"elo\": 1200, \"gamesPlayed\": 0, \"wins\": 0, \"losses\": 0, \"draws\": 0,\n      \"streak\": 0, \"roundsWon\": 0, \"cardsWonTotal\": 0, \"favoriteAttribute\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nextCursor\": null\n}\n```"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Leaderboard - custom page size",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/leaderboard?limit=2",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["leaderboard"],
                            "query": [{ "key": "limit", "value": "2" }]
                        },
                        "description": "Same endpoint, requesting a smaller page. Copy the `nextCursor` value from the response (if it isn't `null`) into the \"Leaderboard - next page\" request below."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "name": "Leaderboard - next page (cursor)",
                    "request": {
                        "method": "GET",
                        "header": [],
                        "url": {
                            "raw": "{{base_url}}/leaderboard?limit=2&cursor=CURSOR_AQUI",
                            "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
                            "path": ["leaderboard"],
                            "query": [
                                { "key": "limit", "value": "2" },
                                { "key": "cursor", "value": "CURSOR_AQUI" }
                            ]
                        },
                        "description": "Replace `CURSOR_AQUI` with the `nextCursor` value returned by the previous page's request."
                    }
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}
